<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Sept adjusted unemployment rises. [CORRECTED 10:55 GMT]</title>
<headline>Pan-German Sept adjusted unemployment rises. [CORRECTED 10:55 GMT]</headline>
<text>
<p>NUREMBERG, Germany, Oct 8 Reuter) - The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Sep 96	Aug 96	     Sep 95</p>
<p> Number (unadj)		3.848 mln   3.902 mln	  3.521 mln</p>
<p> Number (adj)		  3.991 mln   3.952 mln(3.939) 3.669 mln</p>
<p>(Federal Labour Office has revised the adjusted figure for August 1996 to 3.952 million from the 3.939 million published initially).</p>
<p> Change in adj number     +39,000     +21,000	   n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		  10.1 pct    10.2 pct	 9.2 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	  201,186     163,975	  159,258</p>
<p> Vacancies (unadj)	   318,042     331,674	  312,336</p>
<p> Change in numbers in work Jul 96	Jun 96</p>
<p>				  +9,000	 +2,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Previously announced data in brackets. Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>--Bonn Newsroom 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
